<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19841" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆμα</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		 and 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾶμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>step, pace,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				345
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				799
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπουδῇ . . βημάτων πορεύεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					880
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοσόνδε β. διαβεβηκώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					73
				</span></i>
			; <i>footfall</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρατὸν βᾶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					5.17
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς εὔφρονι βήματι
			μολεῖν</span> to journey under the kindly <i>guidance</i> of
			Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				163
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>gait</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. οὐκ ὀρθόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hippiatr.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>step</i>, as a measure of length, =
			<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλαισταί</span>, about <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i> feet, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Deff.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				131
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>step, 'moment'</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόοδος ἐν τρισὶ β. διισταμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					258
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάθρον</span>
			, <i>step, seat</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				193
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>raised place</i> or <i>tribune</i> to speak from in a public
			assembly, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ne.</u>
				8.4
			</span></i>, etc.; in the Pnyx at Athens, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ
				τὸ β. ἀναβῆναι</span> enter <i>public life</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.66
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἀπὸ τοῦ β. ἐλπίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.45
				</span></i>
			; also in the lawcourts, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				48.31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.207
			</span></i>; of a suppliant, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τοῦ β. καθεδούμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					382
				</span></i>
			; in the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλευτήριον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				6.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>tribunal</i> of a magistrate, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἡγεμόνος β.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					434
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμέλη</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.123
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. θεήτρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.239
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>base, pedestal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				219.36
			</span></i> (Ilium, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				299.15
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
